SUMMARY:Dessert Trolley 
LOCATION:The Reading Room
DESCRIPTION:Category: Food & Beverage\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: Avai
 lable\nTime: 7 PM – 10 PM\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/e
 vents/209683\n\nEnd the evening with a nightcap in The Reading Room\, wher
 e The ’Quin’s pastry team presents a beautifully curated dessert troll
 ey in celebration of Hispanic Heritage Month—an elegant showcase of belo
 ved sweets and flavors inspired by traditions from across Latin America.\n
 \nDiscover an assortment of indulgent treats\, from silky flan and delicat
 e alfajores to buttery Mexican wedding cookies\, alongside a rotating sele
 ction of confections thoughtfully crafted for the occasion. Familiar flavo
 rs and time-honored favorites come together with The ’Quin’s signature
  touch\, offering something tempting with every pass of the cart.\n\nWith 
 tableside service and a touch of ceremony\, it’s a sweet celebration of 
 heritage\, tradition\, and the simple pleasure of ending the evening with 
 dessert.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/209683
CATEGORIES:Food & Beverage
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-211490@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261120T143000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261120T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261120T160000
SUMMARY:‘Quin Chat: Inside the Exhibition with Alexandre Gallery
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 3 spots left\nSt
 atus: Waitlist Only\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/21
 1490\n\nJoin us in The Reading Room for a ’Quin Chat exploring the artis
 ts\, influences\, and connections behind our fall exhibition. Phil Alexand
 re\, President & Director of Alexandre Gallery\, joins artist Tessa Greene
  O’Brien for a conversation moderated by The ’Quin’s art collection 
 curator\, Kate Chertavian\, offering fresh perspectives on the works on vi
 ew throughout the ’House.\n\nSpanning the Lobby\, Grand Staircase\, and 
 Reading Room\, the exhibition features 25 works on loan through Alexandre 
 Gallery\, including paintings by Lois Dodd\, Loren MacIver\, Pat Adams\, T
 essa Greene O’Brien\, Lisa Sanditz\, Meghan Brady and Emily Nelligan. To
 gether\, we will explore how these artists translate the world around them
  through distinct approaches to color\, form\, landscape\, and abstraction
  - and consider the shared influences and individual visions that connect 
 their work across generations.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserve
 d for members\, plus one guest. Complimentary light bites and refreshmen
 ts will be served. Cancellations made within 24 hours of the event\, or fa
 ilure to attend\, will result in a $25 charge.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/211490
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
