BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-211944@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261207T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261207T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261207T190000
SUMMARY:Author Talk: "Unspeakable" with Christina Wing
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free\nStatus: Waitlist Only\nEvent U
 RL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/211944\n\n5:00PM Reception\, 5
 :30PM Discussion\n\nSome of the most important conversations are the ones 
 we hesitate to have. Join Harvard Business School faculty member\, Wingspa
 n Legacy Partners founder\, and author Christina Wing for a thoughtful con
 versation with The ’Quin House Co-Founder Sandy Edgerley\, exploring Win
 g’s latest book\, Unspeakable: The Taboo Topics We Avoid and How to Talk
  About Them. From money and succession to failure\, retirement\, and famil
 y dynamics\, Wing examines why certain subjects feel off-limits\, and how 
 avoiding them can quietly undermine trust\, relationships\, and the decisi
 ons that shape our lives.\n\nDrawing on decades of experience across class
 rooms\, boardrooms\, and family enterprises\, Wing will share stories and 
 practical tools for approaching sensitive conversations with clarity\, com
 passion\, and respect. In dialogue with Sandy Edgerley\, she will explore 
 what becomes possible when we move beyond small talk\, offering members fr
 esh perspectives on navigating difficult discussions and building stronger
 \, more honest connections at work and at home.\n\n*This event is complime
 ntary and reserved for members only. Complimentary light bites and refresh
 ments will be served. Cancellations made within 24 hours of the event\, or
  failure to attend\, will result in a $25 charge.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/211944
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-176004@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20261207T183000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261207T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261207T210000
SUMMARY:Serendipity Dinner 
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: Member Mixer\nPrice: $100.00 per person\nAvailability
 : 11 spots left\nStatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhous
 e.com/events/176004\n\nJoin The ’Quin House Director of Membership\, Lis
 a Flores\, for an intimate evening centered around thoughtful conversation
 \, new connections\, and exceptional dining. Over a beautifully curated th
 ree-course dinner with expertly paired wines\, members will be invited to 
 engage in guided conversation designed to spark meaningful exchanges and b
 ring new perspectives to the table.\n\nSettle in\, share stories\, and get
